## Two-photon properties of TP-MOF probes
The TP action cross-section values $(\Phi\delta)^{42-46}$ excited at $820\mathrm{nm}$ were measured to be 137.8 GM for probe 1 reacted with NaHS (Figure 2A), and 99.4 GM for probe 2 reacted with $Z\mathrm{n}^{2+}$ (Figure 2C), and the reaction processes between TP-MOF and target analytes were illustrated in Scheme 2. Figure 2B and Figure 2D displayed the maximum fluorescence emission of reacted probe 1 and probe 2 were $535~\mathrm{nm}$ and $475\ \mathrm{nm}$ , respectively. Besides, the TPA cross section value of unreacted probe 1 and probe 2 were measured to be 32.9 GM (Figure 2A) and 13.2 GM (Figure 2C), respectively. These data suggested that the probes well retained the TP fluorescence properties of the TP fluorophore with negligible fluorescent background from the unreacted probes. Photostability of reacted TP-MOF probes were also investigated under sustaining excitation at $820\mathrm{nm}$ , and within 2 hours, as shown in Figure S1, only $9.5\%$ and $7.5\%$ decreases were observed for probe 1 and probe 2 respectively, which suggested satisfying photostability, avoiding false positive signal resulted from photobleaching.
